# Host tooling lives in `synth-tools`

`synth-core` is a portable `#![no_std]` library. Do **not** add Cargo
`examples/` under `synth-core` for perf harnesses, measurements, generators,
or other host-only utilities.

## Where to put new tools

1. Add a binary at `synth-tools/src/bin/<name>.rs`.
2. Depend on `synth-core` (and any host-only crates) from
   [`synth-tools/Cargo.toml`](synth-tools/Cargo.toml).
3. Run with:

```bash
cargo run --release -p synth-tools --bin <name>
```

## Document every tool

When adding or renaming a binary, update [`synth-tools/README.md`](synth-tools/README.md)
in the same change: short purpose, run command, and any CLI args.

## Anti-patterns

- `synth-core/examples/…` for timing, FFT, file generators, or debug dumps
- `[[bin]]` / `src/bin` inside `synth-core` (keeps host CLIs out of the library crate)
